#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:72
msgid "Auto-Merge Requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:74
msgid ""
"To support running all code through CI, even lightweight contributions, the "
"project employs Mergify to auto-merge pull requests tagged as auto-merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:78
msgid ""
"Use ``hub pull-request -l auto-merge`` to create such a pull request from "
"the command line after pushing a new branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:83
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:85
msgid ""
"The primary tests are run using tox.  Make sure you have tox installed, and "
"invoke it::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:88
msgid "$ tox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:90
msgid ""
"Under continuous integration, additional tests may be run. See the ``.travis."
"yml`` file for full details on the tests run under Travis-CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:95
msgid "Semantic Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:97
msgid "Setuptools follows ``semver``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:103
msgid "Building Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:105
msgid ""
"Setuptools relies on the `Sphinx`_ system for building documentation. The "
"`published documentation`_ is hosted on Read the Docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:108
msgid "To build the docs locally, use tox::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:110
msgid "$ tox -e docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:117
msgid "Vendored Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:119
msgid ""
"Setuptools has some dependencies, but due to `bootstrapping issues <https://"
"github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/980>`_, those dependencies cannot be "
"declared as they won't be resolved soon enough to build setuptools from "
"source. Eventually, this limitation may be lifted as PEP 517/518 reach "
"ubiquitous adoption, but for now, Setuptools cannot declare dependencies "
"other than through ``setuptools/_vendor/vendored.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:127
msgid ""
"All the dependencies specified in these files are \"vendorized\" using a "
"simple Python script ``tools/vendor.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:130
msgid "To refresh the dependencies, run the following command::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:132
msgid "$ tox -e vendor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:137
msgid "Code conventions and other practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:139
msgid ""
"Setuptools utilizes the `skeleton <https://github.com/jaraco/skeleton>`_ "
"framework as a foundation for sharing reusable maintenance tasks across "
"different projects in the ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:143
msgid ""
"This also means that the project adheres to the same coding conventions and "
"other practices described in the `skeleton documentation <https://blog."
"jaraco.com/skeleton/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:147
msgid ""
"Moreover, changes in the code base should be kept as compatible as possible "
"to ``skeleton`` to avoid merge conflicts, or accidental regressions on "
"periodical merges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:151
msgid ""
"Finally, the ``setuptools/_distutils`` directory should not be modified "
"directly when contributing to the ``setuptools`` project. Instead, this "
"directory is maintained as a separated project in https://github.com/pypa/"
"distutils, and periodically merged into ``setuptools``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:159
msgid "Type annotations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:161
msgid ""
"Most standards and best practices are enforced by `Ruff <https://docs.astral."
"sh/ruff/rules/>`_'s ``ANN2``, ``FA``, ``PYI``, ``UP`` and ``YTT`` rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:165
msgid ""
"Explicit return types have to be added for typed public functions whose "
"parameters are *all* annotated. This is enforced by ``ANN2``, but it's worth "
"noting that this is due to mypy inferring ``Any`` even for simple return "
"types. Mypy also doesn't count functions with missing parameter annotations "
"as \"typed\". (see `python/mypy#4409 <https://github.com/python/mypy/"
"issues/4409>`_, `python/mypy#10149 <https://github.com/python/mypy/"
"issues/10149>`_ and `python/mypy#6646 <https://github.com/python/mypy/"
"issues/6646>`_). Otherwise, return annotations can be omitted to reduce "
"verbosity, especially for complex return types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:175
msgid ""
"Instead of typing an explicit return type annotation as ``Generator[..., "
"None, None]``, we'll prefer using an ``Iterator`` as it is more concise and "
"conceptually easier to deal with. Returning a ``Generator`` with no "
"``yield`` type or ``send`` type can sometimes be considered as exposing "
"implementation details. See `Y058 <https://github.com/PyCQA/flake8-pyi/blob/"
"main/ERRORCODES.md#Y058>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../development/developer-guide.rst:182
msgid ""
"Avoid importing private type-checking-only symbols. These are often "
"`typeshed <https://github.com/python/typeshed>`_ internal details and are "
"not guaranteed to be stable. Importing from ``_typeshed`` or "
"``typing_extensions`` is fine, but if you find yourself importing the same "
"symbol in ``TYPE_CHECKING`` blocks a lot, consider implementing an alias "
"directly in ``setuptools``."
msgstr ""
